## Explicitly deferred

Until Gate 1 exits, do not spend the implementation turn on:

- pair-local fan interval projection, ranking, or exclusion variants;
- new ownership or diagnostic taxonomies for existing failures;
- broad test-hygiene cleanup unless it is a compile blocker;
- FlowRep expansion or general patch catalogs;
- seam, close-sheet, cylinder, torus, sphere, thin-tube, mechanical, or bunny-specific logic;
- adaptivity or 2:1 transitions;
- cache, recomputation, memory, scheduler, parallelism, or performance work;
- source-grid recovery enhancement.

## No-progress rule

If two consecutive Code + Build turns do not materially advance the active gate, stop the micro-fix sequence. The next turn must compare the implementation to `DESIGN.md` and produce a bounded design review or replacement proof.

A new diagnostic string, counter, hash, ownership class, or higher aggregate pass count is not material progress by itself.

